body:
@geoand Yeah. I have multiple Quarkus apps and one of them is a middleware between my other apps and D365.
We are using REST clients to make OData API calls on multiple D365 modules (Commerce/CSU, F&O, Inventory visibility, etc).

Some services like Inventory visibility require a token you get by calling the "security service". This is kind of a mess to be honest: First you get a first token. Then POST this token on the security service API, get a 307, POST again on the new URI. The result is another token built from the first one. And this is the token you must use to call other APIs.
